school":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a spell or ability damages multiple things, divide up the damage before applying this effect. This means you can’t normally end up with an odd amount of damage on something.","oracle_id":"68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you have two of these on the battlefield, the damage is multiplied by 4.","oracle_id":"68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The multiplied damage counts in all ways as if it came from the original source. Furnace of Rath is not the source.","oracle_id":"68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The trample rules cause damage to be divided before it is doubled.","oracle_id":"68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple effects modify how damage will be dealt, the player who would be dealt damage or the controller of the creature that would be dealt damage chooses the order to apply the effects. For example, Mending Hands says, “Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.” Suppose a spell would deal 5 damage to a player who has cast Mending Hands targeting themselves. That player can either (a) prevent 4 damage first and then let Furnace of Rath double the remaining 1 damage, taking 2 damage, or (b) double the damage to 10 and then prevent 4 damage, taking 6 damage.","oracle_id":"68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3","published_at":"2005-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage dealt to an opponent usually causes that opponent to lose life. An opponent paying life also causes loss of life.","oracle_id":"8f933fae-6c0c-42d7-a817-14760d8285cd","published_at":"2012-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you and an opponent both lose life simultaneously, and this causes your life total to become 0 or less, you'll lose the game before Exquisite Blood's triggered ability can resolve.","oracle_id":"8f933fae-6c0c-42d7-a817-14760d8285cd","published_at":"2012-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage dealt to an opponent usually causes that opponent to lose life. An opponent paying life also causes loss of life.","oracle_id":"c73c1d91-0163-49c6-832a-b9327e7a2c9b","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card now uses the Reach keyword ability to enable the blocking of flying creatures. This works because a creature with flying can only be blocked by creatures with flying or reach.","oracle_id":"e740ce2f-2134-473c-afa1-1b6d2d1e38ef","published_at":"2008-04-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage dealt to an opponent causes that opponent to lose life. An opponent paying life also causes loss of life.","oracle_id":"fd505c02-c59e-476d-8e88-35da862ddc23","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you and an opponent both lose life simultaneously, and this causes your life total to become 0 or less, you'll lose the game before Bloodthirsty Conqueror's triggered ability can resolve.","oracle_id":"fd505c02-c59e-476d-8e88-35da862ddc23","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
